nodecode-yandex is a rewrite of akinfold's akinfold/hermes-yandex-search-api:

  https://github.com/akinfold/hermes-yandex-search-api
  commit a143ba11735622105d1b762e61c0211e887d4800
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Roman Akinfeev (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is the `hermes_yandex_search` folder at that commit: a
Hermes web-search backend plus one tool, both over Yandex Cloud's Search API
v2. Its wire is carried over unchanged: POST /v2/web/search with
query.searchType, query.queryText, query.page, FAMILY_MODE_MODERATE,
FIX_TYPO_MODE_ON, groupSpec GROUP_MODE_DEEP with groupsOnPage clamped to
1..100 and docsInGroup 1, responseFormat FORMAT_XML, and the Base64 `rawData`
decoded and read for each group's `<doc>` (url, title with its <hlword>
tags flattened, domain, and the passages joined, else the headline); POST
/v2/gen/search with one ROLE_USER message, searchType, fixMisspell, and an
optional site.site list; the `folderId` every body carries; the
`Authorization: Api-Key` header; the answer fields message.content,
sources[].url/title/usedText, searchQueries (objects or bare strings),
fixedMisspellQuery, isAnswerRejected and isBulletAnswer, and the one-element
array a streaming-off answer sometimes arrives in; the refusal read out of a
failed status's message or error member and its details[].requestId; and the
guards in front of the XML — 2 MiB, UTF-8 only, no DTD, a strict Base64. What
the original's own guards did with Expat's version and namespace lengths has
no counterpart here, because this cell scans the document rather than parsing
it, so there is no parser to version-check.

Left out, and why: the harness-level `web_search` backend, because Nodecode
has no such backend to register into — the same search is the
`yandex_web_search` tool and `(yandex:search ...)`; the result envelope's
`position` and `domain` split, which the numbered blocks carry implicitly; and
the optional `region` and `localization` arguments of the original's client,
which its own provider never passed on and no Hermes user could reach. The two
environment variables the plugin manifest required are the section's
`api_key_env` and `folder_id_env`, read the same way (inline first, then the
variable). LICENSE is the repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
